A||N||6||zeelebuba||Pictures Of subwoofer Install (Warning- Not for Purists)||||6||
Z||000000||zeelebuba||12-30-2001||11:20 PM|||| Ok heres my project for the last couple weeks. Started by removing A/C heater core and boxes (I figured what the heck, I have been driving my GTO for years with no heater)<BR> Next I removed the plastic belly and filled it in with tinfoil and made a fiberglass base.<BR> Figured out I had to remove brake booster to get it out - Built a 3/4 mdf top , Formed somes sides out of tinfoil and started fiberglassing the heck out it. When done filled it with correct amount of water and then stuck 2x4 in till water at the top. Then fiberglassed the 2x4 in as reinforcements.<P> Speakers are MTX 12" 5000 powered by a 800 watt amp<P>[img] <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/starting.jpg[/img]" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/starting.jpg[/img]</A> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/unfinisihed_box.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/unfinisihed_box.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/view_of_firewall.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/installed_from_side.jpg"> <P><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000001||zeelebuba||12-31-2001||12:08 AM||||Sorry my wife deleted the pics of the uninstalled finished box||||reg||1
Z||000002||88-DOHC||12-31-2001||01:37 AM||||The problem I have always had with these sort of installations (sealed enclosure in either front or back) is that everyone else can hear it JUST as well as you can.  When I get around to doing my stereo, I am going to have a bandpass box that ports into the cab. Personally for these cars, if you don't have the room or inclination to mount the subs inside the cab, a bandpass box is the only real option for quality bass that won't annoy everyone else on the road. of course if you want everyone else to hear you from 5 blocks away, then this will certainly do it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||yo_sweet||12-31-2001||01:43 AM||||dosent the heat off the rad effect it?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dance.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rearviewgta_1_2_1.jpg">  <P><BR>www.geocities.com/acme_s2000/intro.html<BR>yo_sweet!||||reg||1
Z||000004||zeelebuba||12-31-2001||11:16 AM|||| Well, It dosent actually run so I wont know about the heat thing till summer.<P>  As for the bandpass thing I started thinking about that halfway through the project, and it really does project the sound- I can hear it in the house.<P> Personally I dont like that - I even turn my stereo down when going by people walking on the street, though Im building this car as a highway cruiser..<P> Im thinking of flipping the subs upside down and useing plexiglass on top for second chamber and using 3" ABS ports into the pass compartment- I have to do the math to see if the sizing is there.<P>  Also , Ive never heard a Bandpass before - I would like the bass to be sharper , More defined, A little shorter if that makes sense. Would a Bandpass do that?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Return of Fiero||12-31-2001||01:10 PM||||Audiophile here!!!!!<BR>There was always something about the sub on the front of the Fiero that made the sound level in the car poor.<BR>Even if you used a banpass, or ported design, the sound whas still muffled, or, with the ports, distant and hollow.<P>Best desing I have come up with sounds very good, but takes a LOT of time. It also takes some mods to the rear firewall, but made for a nice competitive system is the standings. just think of 3 JL 10w1-4's (before the 0's were released, firewall pushed back, and two behind the seats, and the ceter console glove box cut out.  Then another 10 in the old glove box place, with the ecm moved under the drivers seat, mounted on thin blocks (to keep it from getting wet. 6 staging speakers,  (pair of 2 way,5 1/4 with 1' neo, 3 way 6',2', and 1' seperates, and a pair of co-ax4'), just so I could play and drive, an inline cross-O mounted in the center console,right by the drivers leg, perfect to play with after shifting, amp rack on the deck lid, (R/F punch 100 and a mac) then there's the alarm...........<P>Sorry about the babbleing, Just love a clean crisp, full experiance in my cars. (drools)<P>Myke||||reg||1
Z||000006||sloth85GT||12-31-2001||09:00 PM||||Why would you mount the subs in the front like that? I can't see it producing any good sound inside the car, just rattling the front hood. Then again, I've never heard one like that, it just doesn't make sense to me. Can you let me know what the pros and cons are of that system?<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">      <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>LT1 Coming Soon.....||||reg||1
